1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,870
Twenty years before German
tanks rolled into Poland,

2
00:00:03,890 --> 00:00:06,617
Germany was not allowed a single tank.

3
00:00:06,637 --> 00:00:09,267
The army was small, the
economy was in ruins,

4
00:00:09,287 --> 00:00:11,104
the country was politically torn apart.

5
00:00:11,124 --> 00:00:14,514
And yet only a few years
later, this very country

6
00:00:14,534 --> 00:00:16,876
led Europe into the
greatest war in history.

7
00:00:16,896 --> 00:00:18,526
How could this happen?

8
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:21,974
In November 1918, the
First World War was lost.

9
00:00:21,994 --> 00:00:25,754
The Kaiser abdicated, and a
republic was proclaimed in Berlin.

10
00:00:25,952 --> 00:00:28,602
Many Germans could not grasp the defeat,

11
00:00:28,622 --> 00:00:31,552
because not a single enemy
soldier stood on German soil.

12
00:00:31,723 --> 00:00:33,673
Soon a lie began to spread:

13
00:00:33,693 --> 00:00:36,023
the army had remained
undefeated in the field

14
00:00:36,043 --> 00:00:38,962
and had been stabbed in the
back by traitors at home.

15
00:00:39,024 --> 00:00:44,133
On 28 June 1919, Germany signed
the Treaty of Versailles.

16
00:00:44,153 --> 00:00:46,423
It lost about one eighth of its territory,

17
00:00:46,443 --> 00:00:50,493
and the Polish Corridor cut East
Prussia off from the rest of the Reich.

18
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:53,292
The army was limited to 100,000 men.

19
00:00:53,312 --> 00:00:56,122
Tanks, an air force and
U-boats were banned,

20
00:00:56,142 --> 00:00:58,557
and the Rhineland was demilitarised.

21
00:00:58,577 --> 00:01:01,677
Germany was held responsible for the war,

22
00:01:01,697 --> 00:01:07,027
and the victors demanded reparations
of 132 billion gold marks.

23
00:01:07,086 --> 00:01:09,646
When Germany fell behind
with its payments,

24
00:01:09,666 --> 00:01:14,281
French and Belgian troops
occupied the Ruhr in 1923.

25
00:01:14,301 --> 00:01:17,251
The government printed money
to pay for the resistance

26
00:01:17,271 --> 00:01:19,825
and set off hyperinflation.

27
00:01:19,845 --> 00:01:25,125
In November 1923, one dollar
cost 4.2 trillion marks,

28
00:01:25,145 --> 00:01:27,614
a loaf of bread in Berlin
hundreds of billions.

29
00:01:27,634 --> 00:01:31,354
Anyone who had saved all their life
was suddenly left with nothing.

30
00:01:31,449 --> 00:01:34,959
That same month in Munich,
a man named Adolf Hitler

31
00:01:34,979 --> 00:01:36,273
tried to seize power.

32
00:01:36,293 --> 00:01:38,663
The putsch collapsed within hours;

33
00:01:38,683 --> 00:01:42,008
Hitler was imprisoned and wrote
his book Mein Kampf there.

34
00:01:42,028 --> 00:01:43,762
Then the tide seemed to turn.

35
00:01:43,782 --> 00:01:46,222
A new currency ended the inflation,

36
00:01:46,242 --> 00:01:49,275
and American loans got the economy going.

37
00:01:49,295 --> 00:01:51,636
But the boom was built on borrowed money.

38
00:01:51,656 --> 00:01:55,696
In October 1929, the New
York stock market crashed.

39
00:01:55,716 --> 00:01:59,696
American banks called in
their loans, factories closed,

40
00:01:59,716 --> 00:02:03,862
and by 1932 six million
Germans were out of work.

41
00:02:03,882 --> 00:02:06,095
The radicals profited.

42
00:02:06,115 --> 00:02:11,680
In 1928 the Nazi Party had won
only 2.6 percent of the vote.

43
00:02:11,700 --> 00:02:18,060
In July 1932, with 37 percent, it became
the largest party in the Reichstag.

44
00:02:18,151 --> 00:02:23,411
On 30 January 1933,
President Paul von Hindenburg

45
00:02:23,431 --> 00:02:25,671
appointed Adolf Hitler Chancellor.

46
00:02:25,776 --> 00:02:29,070
Conservative politicians
believed they could control him.

47
00:02:29,090 --> 00:02:30,358
They were wrong.

48
00:02:30,378 --> 00:02:32,528
Four weeks later the Reichstag burned,

49
00:02:32,548 --> 00:02:36,908
and the very next day key
civil rights were suspended.

50
00:02:37,023 --> 00:02:42,213
With the Enabling Act, the government
could pass laws without parliament.

51
00:02:42,270 --> 00:02:46,060
Trade unions were smashed,
all other parties banned,

52
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:47,940
and the press brought into line.

53
00:02:48,015 --> 00:02:52,255
Jewish shops were boycotted,
Jewish civil servants dismissed.

54
00:02:52,344 --> 00:02:57,574
When Hindenburg died in August 1934,
Hitler also became head of state,

55
00:02:57,594 --> 00:03:01,524
and soldiers had to swear
an oath to him personally.

56
00:03:01,649 --> 00:03:04,890
Germany had been rearming
in secret for years.

57
00:03:04,910 --> 00:03:09,530
In the Soviet Union, far from
Allied inspectors, German officers

58
00:03:09,550 --> 00:03:11,470
trained with tanks and aircraft.

59
00:03:11,556 --> 00:03:13,206
Now it happened openly.

60
00:03:13,293 --> 00:03:17,893
In March 1935 Hitler
reintroduced conscription,

61
00:03:17,913 --> 00:03:21,113
and the Luftwaffe was officially unveiled.

62
00:03:21,168 --> 00:03:24,198
It was a clear breach of
the Treaty of Versailles,

63
00:03:24,218 --> 00:03:26,728
but apart from protests, nothing happened.

64
00:03:26,790 --> 00:03:33,340
On 7 March 1936, German soldiers marched
into the demilitarised Rhineland.

65
00:03:33,464 --> 00:03:38,214
Their retreat had already been planned
in case of a French counterattack.

66
00:03:38,260 --> 00:03:40,300
But France did not intervene.

67
00:03:40,395 --> 00:03:44,245
Hitler later said that the
48 hours after the march-in

68
00:03:44,265 --> 00:03:47,005
were the most nerve-racking of his life.

69
00:03:47,079 --> 00:03:52,229
In March 1938, German troops rolled
across the border into Austria,

70
00:03:52,279 --> 00:03:55,139
and Austria was annexed to the Reich.

71
00:03:55,230 --> 00:03:57,940
Next, Hitler demanded the Sudetenland,

72
00:03:57,960 --> 00:04:01,800
the mainly German-speaking
border regions of Czechoslovakia.

73
00:04:01,877 --> 00:04:06,947
In September 1938, Hitler, Mussolini,

74
00:04:06,967 --> 00:04:11,877
British Prime Minister Chamberlain and
French Premier Daladier met in Munich.

75
00:04:11,928 --> 00:04:15,038
Czechoslovakia itself
had no seat at the table.

76
00:04:15,158 --> 00:04:16,968
Hitler was given the Sudetenland,

77
00:04:16,988 --> 00:04:21,738
and Chamberlain announced in London
that he had brought peace for our time.

78
00:04:21,794 --> 00:04:25,924
A few weeks later, synagogues
burned all over Germany.

79
00:04:25,985 --> 00:04:29,985
In March 1939 the Wehrmacht
marched into Prague,

80
00:04:30,005 --> 00:04:33,675
and Bohemia and Moravia were
declared a protectorate.

81
00:04:33,763 --> 00:04:38,387
Now it was clear that Hitler had never
been after German-speaking lands alone.

82
00:04:38,407 --> 00:04:40,397
Next he demanded Danzig

83
00:04:40,417 --> 00:04:43,807
and a link through the
Corridor to East Prussia.

84
00:04:43,859 --> 00:04:47,779
Britain and France guaranteed
Poland's independence.

85
00:04:47,827 --> 00:04:54,917
But on 23 August 1939, Germany and the
Soviet Union signed a non-aggression pact

86
00:04:54,937 --> 00:05:00,167
and divided Eastern Europe
between them in a secret protocol.

87
00:05:00,256 --> 00:05:06,496
On the evening of 31 August, disguised SS men
attacked the German radio station at Gleiwitz.

88
00:05:06,570 --> 00:05:10,230
The attack was staged,
meant to serve as a pretext.

89
00:05:10,293 --> 00:05:17,343
On 1 September 1939 at 4:45 a.m.,
the battleship Schleswig-Holstein

90
00:05:17,363 --> 00:05:19,743
opened fire on the
Westerplatte near Danzig,

91
00:05:19,763 --> 00:05:23,713
and German troops crossed the
border along a broad front.

92
00:05:23,813 --> 00:05:28,743
Two days later, Britain and
France declared war on Germany.

93
00:05:28,850 --> 00:05:32,810
Twenty years after Versailles,
the Second World War had begun.

94
00:05:33,018 --> 00:05:34,618
It would last six years

95
00:05:34,638 --> 00:05:38,508
and cost more than sixty
million people their lives.
